%% Source: docs/blueprint/BP-07-process-lifecycle.md
%% Diagram: Runtime Ownership and Startup

flowchart TD
    Foreground["jin start --foreground"] --> Check
    Daemon["jin start"] --> Check
    Service["OS service launch"] --> Check

    Check{"existing long-lived owner?"}
    Check -->|service active| ServiceOwned["surface service-owned runtime<br/>do not spawn another daemon"]
    Check -->|daemon or foreground active| AlreadyRunning["surface already-running owner"]
    Check -->|none| Acquire["acquire runtime ownership<br/>lock + PID/state metadata"]

    Acquire --> Store["open store + run SQLite migrations"]
    Store --> Config["load config snapshot for this run"]
    Config --> Build["detect adapters + create sinks"]
    Build --> Boundary["start local control/status boundary"]
    Boundary --> Coordinator["start pipeline coordinator"]
    Coordinator --> Running["runtime running"]

    Desktop["Desktop"] -. uses stable daemon boundary .-> Boundary
    Query["read-only commands"] -. may open store directly without daemon .-> Store
